            "d": "Weil Lkw-Fahrer gesetzlich langsamer reagieren müssen"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "question": "Why does a fully loaded truck need a much longer braking distance than a car at the same speed?",
          "options": {
            "a": "Because trucks are generally fitted with weaker brakes than cars",
            "b": "Because kinetic energy increases with mass, so more energy must be dissipated to stop",
            "c": "Because truck tyres are made of softer rubber",
